      "writtenOn": "2025-07-29T03:33:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So the naming variance \"update_cpufreq_...\" and \"cpufreq_update_...\" feels a little inconsistent. Would it be worth a cleanup patch aligning them? Or somehow better differentiate the naming? (as update_cpufreq_current-\u003e__update_cpufreq_ctx_switch-\u003ecpufreq_update_util(), it feels like you\u0027ve got \"go do the tangled path, and the direct call\"). It seems like this should be flattened somehow.",
      "revId": "e011c0ccc7e2b85779a9245a1b1a02eb68a68bff",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "07124fc0_22db6da7",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/syscalls.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 786,
      "author": {
        "id": 1976445
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-08T15:27:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Isn\u0027t this out-of-scopre for a FROMLIST patch? I tried to follow as many of your suggestions to clean up; but it feels this goes beyond the necessity bits to apply a FROMLIST patch given no correctness issues.\n\nIt is very subjective whether this is inconsistent. I acknowledge your point view and will think how can accomodate that in future upstream postings; but from my view `cpufreq_` prefix indicates this is a exported cpufreq function, which it is. If I use the same prefix in the scheduler it\u0027ll be inconsistent and confusing. `update_cpufreq_..` indicates we are performing an action on cpufreq interface and current. Naming is hard and I am sure someone else will find them confusing.\n\n\u003e  it feels like you\u0027ve got \"go do the tangled path, and the direct call\"). It seems like this should be flattened somehow.\n\nI didn\u0027t understand this. update_cpufreq_current() is called from two places and directly calling __update_cpufreq_ctx_switch() is possible but this is not a context switch and you\u0027d have to have a long comment explaining why you\u0027re doing a context switch activity in non context switch. The wrapper, in my view, makes this self documented.\n\nWe could add yet another wrapper maybe to abstract the running logic, from my view that was not necessary to add further wrappers as we do the running/queued logic in many places this way and this form seemed more consistent.",
      "parentUuid": "fd961fa7_48fdce20",
      "revId": "e011c0ccc7e2b85779a9245a1b1a02eb68a68bff",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
